cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Verifiable mechanistic interpretability by grading explanations using simulations"
abstract: >-
  An explanation of a trained modular-addition transformer is graded by having a weights-blind, offline local LLM
  agent rebuild the network's weights from the explanation alone, then comparing the replacement with the original
  by output KL divergence and symmetry-aware hidden-state similarity. Developed in a mechanistic interpretability
  hackathon on automatically evaluating mechanistic interpretability explanations, co-organized by the authors in
  their mechanistic interpretability community (https://mechinterp.com/).
authors:
